{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Stop using public money to fund animal experiments",
        "additional_details": "Recently released footage of dogs, primates, pigs, rats and rabbits subjected to highly invasive procedures has exposed the distressing reality of animal testing in UK laboratories.\r\n\r\nRedirecting government investment towards cutting-edge, animal-free technologies could help establish the UK as a global leader, accelerate medical and scientific progress, and spare millions of animals from suffering.",
        "background": "The Government must end public funding for animal experiments and instead fund the development and adoption of human-relevant, non-animal research methods. We feel this is essential to deliver the Government's Replacing Animals in Science strategy and end the suffering of animals in laboratories.",
        "closed_at": null,
        "closing_date": "2027-04-29",
